The purpose of documentation:

Documentation is normally made for the following types of readers:

1. Other data engineers, team members and future colleagues. 
2. Data product owner.
2. End users, stakeholders, analists.
4. AI agents.

Each reader has different purpose and requirements. 

| reader    |  purpose         | 
---------------------------------
| Data engineers | maintain and extend the data object | 
| Data product owner | functional maintenance, communicate with stakeholders |
| End users, stakeholders, analists | Understand business definitions. How are column values constructed out of source data? which filters are applied, which assumptions were made and which business rules were executed. This
is needed when using this data object for a reporting or analytics task. E.g. for determining whether this 
data object is suitable for answering certain questions.|
| AI agents | What is the purpose of this data object and how should it be populated from source dat. Unambiguous specification |
----------------------------------------

